01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The Wolf of Wall Street is a 2013 American epic biographical dark comedy crime film co-produced and directed
by Martin Scorsese, written by Terence Winter, and based on Jordan Belfort's 2007 memoir.

12
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
It loosely recounts Belfort's career as a stockbroker in New York City and how his firm, Stratton
Oakmont, engaged in rampant corruption and fraud on Wall Street, leading to his downfall.

13
01:10:54,545 --> 01:11:00,545
The film stars Leonardo DiCaprio as Belfort; Jonah Hill as his business partner and friend Donnie Azoff; Margot Robbie as his second wife, Naomi Lapaglia;
Matthew McConaughey as his mentor and former boss Mark Hanna; and Kyle Chandler as FBI special agent Patrick Denham portraying Gregory Coleman.

14
01:16:21,818 --> 01:16:27,818
It is DiCaprio's fifth collaboration with Scorsese.

15
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
DiCaprio and Warner Bros.

16
01:27:16,363 --> 01:27:22,363
acquired the rights to Belfort's memoir in 2007, but
production was halted due to content restrictions.

17
01:32:43,636 --> 01:32:49,636
It was later produced by the independent Red Granite Pictures.

18
01:38:10,909 --> 01:38:16,909
The film was shot in New York in late 2012, using mostly 35mm film stock.

19
01:43:38,181 --> 01:43:44,181
The film premiered in New York City on December 17, 2013, and was released
in the United States on December 25, by Paramount Pictures.

20
01:49:05,454 --> 01:49:11,454
It was the first major American film to be released
exclusively through digital distribution.

21
01:54:32,727 --> 01:54:38,727
It was a major commercial success, grossing $407 million worldwide during its
theatrical run, becoming Scorsese's highest-grossing film.

22
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
However, the film initially received considerable controversy for its moral ambiguity and lack of sympathy for victims, as well as its explicit, graphic sexual
content, extreme profanity (with at least 500 uses of the expletive "fuck"), depiction of hard drug use, and use of animals during production.

23
02:05:27,272 --> 02:05:33,272
The film was initially rated NC-17 by the Motion Picture Association of America, but it was
shortly appealed for an R rating after Scorsese made slight changes to the film.

24
02:10:54,545 --> 02:11:00,545
It set a Guinness World Record for the most instances of profanity in a film.

25
02:16:21,818 --> 02:16:27,818
The film's financing became implicated in the 1Malaysia
Development Berhad corruption scandal; the U.S.

26
02:21:49,090 --> 02:21:55,090
Department of Justice and the Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission investigated
Red Granite Pictures, and producer Riza Aziz was arrested in 2019.

27
02:27:16,363 --> 02:27:22,363
He was discharged in May 2020 on a 1,000,000
Malaysian ringgit (US$240,000) bail.

28
02:32:43,636 --> 02:32:49,636
The film received positive reviews from critics and
appeared on several "best of the year" lists.

29
02:38:10,909 --> 02:38:16,909
It was nominated for several awards, including five at the 86th Academy Awards ceremony: Best Picture, Best
Director, Best Adapted Screenplay, Best Actor (for DiCaprio) and Best Supporting Actor (for Hill).

30
02:43:38,181 --> 02:43:44,181
DiCaprio won Best Actor – Musical or Comedy at the 71st Golden Globe Awards, where
the film was also nominated for Best Picture – Musical or Comedy.

31
02:49:05,454 --> 02:49:11,454
The film explores themes of corruption, based on novel or
book, drug addiction, anti hero, con man.

32
02:54:32,727 --> 02:54:38,727
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and intense.
